# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 4 — G2: `g0_unguarded.ebnf` plus a STRUCTURAL follow guard.
#
# ⛔ ONE-DIFFERENCE CONTROL, against BOTH neighbours. Byte-for-byte `g0_unguarded.ebnf` except for
# the `prim` line; and byte-for-byte `g1_byte_guard.ebnf` except for what the lookahead wraps.
#
#   G0:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix )*
#   G1:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &residual_first_byte )*            byte set { ' , / }
#   G2:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &( tick lparen lit rparen ) )*     the residual ITSELF
#
# WHAT IT MODELS. Slice 2's mandated refinement — *"a trivia-aware structural lookahead
# (`&( residual )` — exact, at the price of a per-iteration sub-parse instead of one byte compare)"*.
# The lookahead's body is the holder's residual verbatim, so the guard asks the only question that
# is actually decidable: *can the holder's residual parse here?* — not *does the next byte look like
# it might?*
#
# ⭐ WHY IT IS TRIVIA-AWARE FOR FREE. The guard is a normal sub-parse
# (`generate_lookahead_logic`, `ast_based_generator.rs:4120` — `try_parse`, then restore
# `parser.position`), so `tick := trivia "'"` runs its own `trivia` exactly as it would in the real
# parse. Nothing here is layout-specific; the exactness is a consequence of reusing the parser
# instead of approximating it.
#
# ⛔ AND WHY IT IS NOT FREE. One sub-parse of the residual per committed iteration, on the
# SUCCESS path, versus one byte compare. That is the cost `.17`'s acceptance (a) requires priced
# against PGEN's second non-negotiable, and it is the reason G1 exists in this bank at all: if the
# cheap form sufficed, the expensive one would not be bought.
@entry: true
scratch := kw_k eq outer_cast semi
outer_cast := ct tick lparen lit rparen
ct := kw | prim
prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &( tick lparen lit rparen ) )*
prim_base := lit | cast_seed
cast_seed := kw tick lparen lit rparen
prim_suffix := tick lparen lit rparen

lit := trivia /n/
kw := trivia /t/
kw_k := trivia /k/
eq := trivia "="
semi := trivia ";"
tick := trivia "'"
lparen := trivia "("
rparen := trivia ")"

@branch_policy: priority_first
trivia := (line_comment | block_comment)*
line_comment := /\/\/[^\n]*(\n|$)/
block_comment := /\/\*([^*]|\*+[^*\/])*\*+\//
